From 3ce916aa05e4279a2f76ddbc5d333153458475e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vair <79313360+nicolasvair@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:49:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(record): arming a destination that is already recording
 does not punch it out (objekat 0048)

InputDeviceInstance::updateRecordingStatus runs on an async update, one message-loop turn
after valueTreePropertyChanged(armed / targetID). When the record was started in the same
turn as the arm, the destination is already recording when the update runs: it was stopped
(prepareToStopRecording + stopRecording) and only restarted when that stop produced no clip.
Once more than ~10 ms had been written the clip existed, nothing restarted, and the input
stopped recording while the transport went on (a take of exactly one block when the main
thread was late). A destination that is armed AND already recording is now left alone.
Disarming, and a destination that is not recording, behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../playback/devices/tracktion_InputDevice.cpp     | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/devices/tracktion_InputDevice.cpp b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/devices/tracktion_InputDevice.cpp
index c0675a36e4d..979f667cdb9 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/devices/tracktion_InputDevice.cpp
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/devices/tracktion_InputDevice.cpp
@@ -264,6 +264,20 @@ void InputDeviceInstance::updateRecordingStatus()
         if (! track)
             continue;
 
+        // objekat 0048: arming a destination that is already recording (the record was started in the
+        // same message-loop turn as the arm, so this deferred update only runs once the take is under
+        // way) must not punch it out. The stop below would end the take, and the restart only happens
+        // when the stop produced no clip: after more than ~10 ms the clip exists, nothing restarts, and
+        // the input stays silent while the transport carries on.
+        if (isRecordingEnabled (targetID) && isRecording (targetID))
+        {
+            if (destinationsChanged)
+                restartPlayback = true;
+
+            wasLivePlayActive = isLivePlayEnabled (*track);
+            continue;
+        }
+
         InputDeviceInstance::StopRecordingParameters params;
         params.targetsToStop = { targetID };
         params.unloopedTimeToEndRecording = context.getUnloopedPosition();
